  "user_request_original": "Optimize an 8-layer planar dielectric stack on a semi-infinite Silicon substrate. Incident medium is Air. Illumination is normal incidence (0 deg), unpolarized. Wavelength bands are 1260-1360 nm and 1530-1565 nm. Materials are SiO2 (Lemarchand) and Ta2O5 (Gao). Stack sequence from Air to Si: SiO2 (Lemarchand), Ta2O5 (Gao), SiO2 (Lemarchand), Ta2O5 (Gao), SiO2 (Lemarchand), Ta2O5 (Gao), SiO2 (Lemarchand), Ta2O5 (Gao). Initialize layer thicknesses to [185.61, 59.80, 57.89, 140.33, 216.18, 117.31, 31.71, 33.20] nm. Apply a random isotropic perturbation of ±25 nm to each layer thickness before optimization, ensuring final thicknesses remain within 20-400 nm. Use a gradient-based thickness optimizer to minimize the average reflectance across both bands simultaneously. Report best_target_score, valid_candidates, tightest_margin, run_status, and thicknesses_nm.",
